# Keeps the deployment under the Hobby plan's 12 serverless function limit.
# linkedin-seed.js is superseded by linkedin-refresh.js (the deck's Sync button calls
# refresh, which inserts missing rows without deleting anything). The file stays in the
# repo for reference but is not deployed.
api/linkedin-seed.js

# The eight handlers below were consolidated behind api/linkedin/[action].js, which is a
# single serverless function. Each one was copied byte for byte to api/_lk_<action>.js
# (files starting with "_" are not routes, so they cost nothing) and vercel.json rewrites
# every original /api/linkedin-<action> URL to the router. The originals stay in the repo
# as a reference for one release, but must NOT be deployed: each one Vercel sees here
# costs a function slot, and eight of them put the deployment back over the limit.
#
# Once the router has run in production for a cycle these nine files can be deleted
# outright. Nothing imports them.
api/linkedin-decide.js
api/linkedin-dispatch.js
api/linkedin-emails.js
api/linkedin-health.js
api/linkedin-posts.js
api/linkedin-refresh.js
api/linkedin-remind.js
api/linkedin-translate.js

# Superseded by api/linkedin.js. The router used to live at api/linkedin/[action].js and
# that function was missing from production entirely: /api/linkedin-posts AND the direct
# /api/linkedin/posts both returned the SPA's index.html with a 200, which is what you get
# when no function matches and the catch-all rewrite takes over. Every other function was
# live at the time, so it was not a build failure and not the rewrites.
#
# Square brackets are glob metacharacters and get mangled by enough tooling that betting
# the LinkedIn surface on one bracketed filename in a nested folder was a bad trade. The
# router is now a plain file at the api root and the action arrives as a query parameter.
#
# This file is ignored rather than deleted because deleting is not something this session
# can do. Delete api/linkedin/ by hand once the new router has run for a cycle.
api/linkedin/[action].js

# The /internal Studio deck is retired. Its page is now a stub that points at
# /internal-pratik, so these three functions have no caller left. They are ignored rather
# than deleted because studio_packages still holds its 100 rows and restoring the deck
# should stay a matter of reverting one file. Ignoring them also frees three function slots,
# which is what makes room for api/fb.js without going back over the Hobby plan limit.
api/internal-packages.js
api/internal-decide.js
api/internal-reset.js
